{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaxUmLNmzHCxxkzpw7sc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've replaced the `sorry` with a proof, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\n`fibState_correct` can't be proved by induction on `n` directly, because each step changes the starting values from `0, 1` to other pairs. So I added a more general helper lemma to `Main.lean`:\n\n```lean\ntheorem fibState_gen (n k : Nat) :\n    fibState n (fibN k) (fibN (k + 1)) = (fibN (n + k), fibN (n + k + 1))\n```\n\n- **Helper lemma:** proved by induction on `n`, letting `k` vary. Each step uses the fact that `fibN k + fibN (k + 1)` is `fibN (k + 2)` by definition, applies the induction hypothesis at `k + 1`, and uses `omega` to show `n + (k + 1) = n + 1 + k`.\n- **`fibState_correct`:** is the helper with `k = 0`, since `fibN 0 = 0` and `fibN 1 = 1`; `simpa [fibN]` finishes it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":756,"cache_read_input_tokens":8000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":756},"output_tokens":356,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0cadf3b2-8cf0-47d5-8f49-13cf802eee9a","uuid":"98ce0d4f-b8ea-43c4-856c-8af2dea2b34d","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:37:04.026Z","request_id":"req_011CgaxUm8DwGiqMgJkPehAT"}
